From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:49:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 096/117] drm/msm: fail the queued submits when the GPU does
 not recover

recover_worker() replays every queued submit after ->recover(), even when
the hardware init at the end of ->recover() failed and the GPU is still
down (on Adreno 8xx: a GMU that no longer boots). Each replayed submit then
hangs again and is dropped only one hangcheck period later, so the fences
of a busy client stay pending for minutes: the compositor stalls, atomic
commits wait on their in-fences, and system suspend and shutdown wait on
the GPU.

When ->recover() leaves the GPU needing a hardware init, complete the
queued submits with -EIO instead of replaying them and count a fault on
their queues, as a8xx_drop_queued_submits() already does when the CX
collapse fails. The next submit runs the hardware init again through
runtime resume, so a GPU that comes back later is used again.

Problem and approach found by Travis Geisinger, in linux-perpetua
commit 615157350526 ("drm/msm: Fail the pending submits when the GPU does not recover")
(no Signed-off-by); re-implemented on our A8xx recovery code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
index 3b48b6b6e4747..54093ce9b4c97 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -484,6 +484,44 @@ static void get_comm_cmdline(struct msm_gem_submit *submit, char **comm, char **
 	put_task_struct(task);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Called with gpu->lock held after ->recover() when the hardware init at its
+ * end failed: the GPU is still not running, so replaying the queued submits
+ * would only hang each of them again, a full hangcheck period apiece, while
+ * everybody waiting on their fences (compositor, atomic commits, system
+ * suspend and shutdown) waits with them. Complete them with -EIO instead and
+ * count a fault on their queues. The next submit runs the hardware init again
+ * through runtime resume, so a GPU that comes back later is used again.
+ */
+static void fail_queued_submits(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
+{
+	unsigned int i, n = 0;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < gpu->nr_rings; i++) {
+		struct msm_ringbuffer *ring = gpu->rb[i];
+		u32 fence = ring->fctx->last_fence;
+		struct msm_gem_submit *submit;
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&ring->submit_lock, flags);
+		list_for_each_entry(submit, &ring->submits, node) {
+			if (!fence_after(submit->seqno, ring->memptrs->fence))
+				continue;
+			dma_fence_set_error(submit->hw_fence, -EIO);
+			submit->queue->faults++;
+			n++;
+		}
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ring->submit_lock, flags);
+
+		ring->memptrs->fence = fence;
+		msm_update_fence(ring->fctx, fence);
+	}
+
+	DRM_DEV_ERROR(gpu->dev->dev,
+		      "%s: GPU not recovered: %u queued submit(s) failed, not replayed\n",
+		      gpu->name, n);
+}
+
 static void recover_worker(struct kthread_work *work)
 {
 	struct msm_gpu *gpu = container_of(work, struct msm_gpu, recover_work);
@@ -584,6 +622,10 @@ static void recover_worker(struct kthread_work *work)
 
 	gpu->funcs->recover(gpu);
 
+	/* ->recover() ends with a hardware init: did the GPU come back? */
+	if (gpu->needs_hw_init)
+		fail_queued_submits(gpu);
+
 	/* retire completed submits, plus the one that hung: */
 	retire_submits(gpu);
 
-- 
